{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>You shall celebrate.</b> You shall slaughter the slaughter, and the meaning concerns the congregation. Or the meaning is: you shall celebrate, as an individual, by bringing burnt offerings and peace offerings. And the proof is \"for He will bless you,\" the meaning being: you shall do this because HaShem blessed you. And He added \"in all your produce\" to explain the blessing of the produce that the earth brought forth." "<b>The work of your hands.</b> In trade and craft." "<b>And you shall be altogether joyful.</b> It is a commandment to rejoice on the festival of Sukkot. And some say: \"for He will bless you\" refers to the future, and you will be eternally joyful." "And the meaning of <b>only.</b> For you will be nothing but thus."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:43.313710686Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}